# What goes into the Genie image for QA and prod: ONLY what the service runs on.
#
# Allowlist, not denylist: everything is excluded, then the runtime is let back in.
# A new dev script, test, notebook or secret added anywhere tomorrow stays out of
# the image without anyone remembering to list it here.
#
# The service needs:
#   service/genie/           the code
#   service/requirements.txt its dependencies
#   ontology/, catalog/      read at startup (genie_ontology_root) and validated
#
# Deliberately left out: service/scripts/ (ask.py, dev_login.py), service/tests/,
# tools/, tests/, kb/, reference/, asks/, docs, .env, secrets/, .cache/.

*

!service/genie/
!service/requirements.txt
!ontology/
!catalog/

# Never, even inside an allowed folder.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/*.jwt
**/*.token
**/.env
**/.env.*
